# Environment variables for the Claude Code cloud environment of exucal.
#
# KEEP IN SYNC: the cloud environment's "Environment variables" field
# (claude.ai/code, environment settings) holds a pasted copy of the
# assignments below, one KEY=VALUE per line. It is not read from the
# repository. When this file changes, update the field too, and vice versa.
# scripts/cloud-setup.sh (the setup script) and .claude/hooks/session-start.sh
# (the per-session hook) are the other two parts; README.md ("Cloud
# environment") describes how they fit together.
#
# The project needs no variable to build, test or run: the toolchain is on
# PATH through the SessionStart hook, and the settings that matter are in
# files the tools read on their own (pnpm-workspace.yaml for pnpm, .env for
# wrangler). What is deliberately absent, so that nobody adds it back:
#
#   PATH                  Not here. The hook prepends /opt/node24/bin for the
#                         session; a literal PATH set here would freeze the
#                         base image's directories and break when they move.
#   WRANGLER_SEND_METRICS Already `false` in .env, which wrangler reads from
#                         the project root on every command.
#   CI                    Not set. The lockfile is frozen for every install
#                         by pnpm-workspace.yaml, so CI=true would add
#                         nothing there and changes the output of other
#                         tools (vite, wrangler) for no gain.
#   Secrets and tokens    Never. Nothing the project runs needs one, and a
#                         deploy is done from a developer's machine (README.md,
#                         "Deployment"), not from a cloud session.
#
# The one assignment is a policy setting, not a requirement: the console
# telemetry opt-out that tools honor by convention (wrangler among them, as
# the comment in .env notes), kept alongside the repository's other telemetry
# opt-outs so that a cloud session is silent in the same way a developer's
# machine is asked to be.
DO_NOT_TRACK=1
